infonl__podiumd-minikube	R148	Keep `cli.py` limited to parsing arguments and calling the logic.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R149	When adding a near-copy of existing code, merge it with the original in the same change, even if the copies differ only in a detail.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R150	When splitting or moving code, also merge the pieces that do the same thing.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R151	Never leave a wrapper that only forwards to another function.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R152	Keep `bin/<command>` as symlinks to `bin/.stub` so old command names keep working.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R153	A value that several places need (a host, a URL, a port, a credential) must come from one place.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R154	Source a shared value from `values.yaml` or one generated list.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R155	Before committing, ensure `./run_python_checks` passes, including jscpd and vulture.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R156	Review new comments, help texts and messages against [[comments-and-help-texts]] before committing.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R157	Before committing, review the diff for where else the same concept is computed.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R158	For each new function, script or template, search for the same concept by its low-level calls.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R159	Preferably do that duplicate search with a review subagent that has not seen the change being written.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R160	Name in the commit message the existing helpers that were checked, and which one was extended or why none fit.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R161	Do not write tests that check how PodiumD's applications behave.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R162	Make each new live test assert something this project's code makes true, such as a fixup applied, a Job or Secret the deploy creates, a limit set, or the edge's routes.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R163	In a live test, a single HTTP call into an application is allowed when it is the only way to verify something this project's code makes true.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R164	Never write a functional scenario against a PodiumD application in a live test.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R165	Send an application check (login flows, API behaviour, mail, forms, app health) to podiumd-tests instead of adding it to this project's tests.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R166	After a deploy, run `podiumd-tests run --env minikube --tier smoke` to check that the applications answer.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R167	Ensure every object has exactly one managing repository, and never let two repositories both create or prune the same object.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R168	Manage the components and their wiring, the edge and its routes, the Keycloak clients and client roles in the realm config, the Open Notificaties kanalen in values.yaml, and the opt-in Frank!Gateway with OpenBao in this project.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R169	Do not create test users, test clients and tokens, realm roles, the DigiD/eHerkenning OIDC configuration, Open Inwoner CMS pages and contact form, Open Formulieren test forms, or further kanalen.
infonl__podiumd-minikube	R170	Do not manage eSuite or Alertmanager routes from either repository.

